    "engine": "jupyter",
    "markdown": "---\ntitle: \"Exploratory Data Analysis\"\nsubtitle: \"AI vs. Non-AI Careers in 2024 Job Postings\"\nauthor:\n  - name: Hye Won Kim\n    affiliations:\n      - id: bu\n        name: Boston University\n        city: Boston\n        state: MA\nbibliography: references.bib\ncsl: csl/econometrica.csl\nformat:\n  html:\n    toc: true\n    number-sections: true\n    df-print: paged\nexecute:\n  freeze: auto\n---\n\n## Exploratory Data Analysis\n\nThis section explores the 2024 Lightcast job postings dataset to compare AI-related and non-AI careers. Since our research topic focuses on **AI vs. Non-AI Careers**, the visualizations focus on career areas, industries, and skills associated with AI-related job postings.\n\n::: {#5c5dea9c .cell execution_count=1}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nimport pandas as pd\nimport plotly.express as px\nimport re\n\nuse_cols = [\n    \"TITLE_RAW\",\n    \"TITLE_NAME\",\n    \"TITLE_CLEAN\",\n    \"SKILLS_NAME\",\n    \"SPECIALIZED_SKILLS_NAME\",\n    \"COMMON_SKILLS_NAME\",\n    \"SOFTWARE_SKILLS_NAME\",\n    \"LOT_CAREER_AREA_NAME\",\n    \"LOT_OCCUPATION_NAME\",\n    \"NAICS_2022_2_NAME\",\n    \"REMOTE_TYPE_NAME\"\n]\n\ndf = pd.read_csv(\"cleaned_lightcast_jobs.csv\", usecols=use_cols)\n\ndf.shape\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=1}\n```\n(69198, 11)\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\n### Creating an AI-Related Job Indicator\n\nBefore creating the visualizations, postings were classified into AI-related and non-AI categories. The cleaned dataset does not include a direct variable that identifies whether a posting is AI-related, so a rule-based indicator was created.\n\nTo make this classification more data-driven, the job title and skill fields were reviewed before finalizing the keyword list. This review showed that broad search terms such as “AI,” “learning,” “language,” “vision,” and “model” captured many unrelated postings, including retail, claims, supply chain, learning management systems, speech language roles, supervision, provisioning, and data modeling. Therefore, these broad terms were not used by themselves.\n\nThe final AI-related indicator uses more specific AI and machine learning terms observed in the dataset, including Artificial Intelligence, Generative Artificial Intelligence, AI/ML, ML/AI, Machine Learning, MLOps, Deep Learning, Reinforcement Learning, Artificial Neural Networks, Computer Vision, Large Language Model, LLM, Predictive Modeling, and Predictive Analytics.\n\n::: {#6e2cc56b .cell execution_count=2}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nai_keywords = [\n    \"artificial intelligence\",\n    \"generative artificial intelligence\",\n    \"ai/ml\",\n    \"ml/ai\",\n    \"machine learning\",\n    \"machine learning algorithms\",\n    \"machine learning model training\",\n    \"machine learning data scientist\",\n    \"machine learning data engineer\",\n    \"mlops\",\n    \"deep learning\",\n    \"reinforcement learning\",\n    \"artificial neural networks\",\n    \"recurrent neural network\",\n    \"convolutional neural networks\",\n    \"computer vision\",\n    \"large language model\",\n    \" llm \",\n    \"predictive modeling\",\n    \"predictive analytics\"\n]\n\ntext_cols = [\n    \"TITLE_RAW\",\n    \"TITLE_NAME\",\n    \"TITLE_CLEAN\",\n    \"SKILLS_NAME\",\n    \"SPECIALIZED_SKILLS_NAME\",\n    \"COMMON_SKILLS_NAME\",\n    \"SOFTWARE_SKILLS_NAME\"\n]\n\ncombined_text = df[text_cols].fillna(\"\").agg(\" \".join, axis=1).str.lower()\n\npattern = \"|\".join([re.escape(keyword) for keyword in ai_keywords])\n\ndf[\"AI_RELATED\"] = combined_text.str.contains(pattern, regex=True)\ndf[\"Career Type\"] = df[\"AI_RELATED\"].map({True: \"AI-Related\", False: \"Non-AI\"})\n\ndf[\"Career Type\"].value_counts()\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=2}\n```\nCareer Type\nNon-AI        61674\nAI-Related     7524\nName: count, dtype: int64\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\n## AI-Related vs. Non-AI Job Postings by Career Area\n\nThis visualization compares AI-related and non-AI postings across major career areas. It was chosen because our project asks how AI may affect different fields. By comparing career areas, we can identify where AI-related hiring demand is more visible and whether AI-related jobs are concentrated in technical fields or spread across broader business and professional areas.\n\n::: {#8d533279 .cell execution_count=3}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\ncareer_area_counts = (\n    df.groupby([\"LOT_CAREER_AREA_NAME\", \"Career Type\"])\n    .size()\n    .reset_index(name=\"Job Postings\")\n)\n\ntop_career_areas = (\n    df[\"LOT_CAREER_AREA_NAME\"]\n    .dropna()\n    .value_counts()\n    .head(12)\n    .index\n)\n\ncareer_area_counts = career_area_counts[\n    career_area_counts[\"LOT_CAREER_AREA_NAME\"].isin(top_career_areas)\n]\n\nfig = px.bar(\n    career_area_counts,\n    x=\"Job Postings\",\n    y=\"LOT_CAREER_AREA_NAME\",\n    color=\"Career Type\",\n    barmode=\"group\",\n    orientation=\"h\",\n    title=\"AI-Related vs. Non-AI Job Postings by Career Area\",\n    labels={\n        \"LOT_CAREER_AREA_NAME\": \"Career Area\",\n        \"Job Postings\": \"Number of Job Postings\"\n    }\n)\n\nfig.update_layout(yaxis={\"categoryorder\": \"total ascending\"})\nfig.show()\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display}\n```{=html}\n<div style=\"height:525px; width:100%;\">            <script src=\"https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/mathjax/2.7.5/MathJax.js?config=TeX-AMS-MML_SVG\"></script><script>if (window.MathJax && window.MathJax.Hub && window.MathJax.Hub.Config) {window.MathJax.Hub.Config({SVG: {font: \"STIX-Web\"}});}</script>                <script>window.PlotlyConfig = {MathJaxConfig: 'local'};</script>\n        <script charset=\"utf-8\" src=\"https://cdn.plot.ly/plotly-3.6.0.min.js\" integrity=\"sha256-QaOVwtVY0T02VaHrr6pnoHLCwayMJp4O5n4YyaE3rJk=\" crossorigin=\"anonymous\"></script>                <div id=\"27217e37-61dd-4d76-9995-24b0b0d6f700\" class=\"plotly-graph-div\" style=\"height:100%; width:100%;\"></div>            <script>                window.PLOTLYENV=window.PLOTLYENV || {};                                if (document.getElementById(\"27217e37-61dd-4d76-9995-24b0b0d6f700\")) {                    Plotly.newPlot(                        \"27217e37-61dd-4d76-9995-24b0b0d6f700\",                        [{\"alignmentgroup\":\"True\",\"hovertemplate\":\"Career Type=AI-Related\\u003cbr\\u003eNumber of Job Postings=%{x}\\u003cbr\\u003eCareer Area=%{y}\\u003cextra\\u003e\\u003c\\u002fextra\\u003e\",\"legendgroup\":\"AI-Related\",\"marker\":{\"color\":\"#636efa\",\"pattern\":{\"shape\":\"\"}},\"name\":\"AI-Related\",\"offsetgroup\":\"AI-Related\",\"orientation\":\"h\",\"showlegend\":true,\"textposition\":\"auto\",\"x\":{\"dtype\":\"i2\",\"bdata\":\"2AAMAHEcDwA=\"},\"xaxis\":\"x\",\"y\":[\"Business Management and Operations\",\"Healthcare\",\"Information Technology and Computer Science\",\"Marketing and Public Relations\"],\"yaxis\":\"y\",\"type\":\"bar\"},{\"alignmentgroup\":\"True\",\"hovertemplate\":\"Career Type=Non-AI\\u003cbr\\u003eNumber of Job Postings=%{x}\\u003cbr\\u003eCareer Area=%{y}\\u003cextra\\u003e\\u003c\\u002fextra\\u003e\",\"legendgroup\":\"Non-AI\",\"marker\":{\"color\":\"#EF553B\",\"pattern\":{\"shape\":\"\"}},\"name\":\"Non-AI\",\"offsetgroup\":\"Non-AI\",\"orientation\":\"h\",\"showlegend\":true,\"textposition\":\"auto\",\"x\":{\"dtype\":\"i4\",\"bdata\":\"pA8AAPUAAAC33wAAiQAAABEAAAA=\"},\"xaxis\":\"x\",\"y\":[\"Business Management and Operations\",\"Healthcare\",\"Information Technology and Computer Science\",\"Marketing and Public Relations\",\"Unknown\"],\"yaxis\":\"y\",\"type\":\"bar\"}],                        {\"template\":{\"data\":{\"histogram2dcontour\":[{\"type\":\"histogram2dcontour\",\"colorbar\":{\"outlinewidth\":0,\"ticks\":\"\"},\"colorscale\":[[0.0,\"#0d0887\"],[0.1111111111111111,\"#46039f\"],[0.2222222222222222,\"#7201a8\"],[0.3333333333333333,\"#9c179e\"],[0.4444444444444444,\"#bd3786\"],[0.5555555555